34,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,May,,"Well, it's official. One person has been suffering in silence—or rather, complaining loudly—while we just walked past. The space distribution is totally uneven.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I've seen that ""better"" solutions can be traps. The station block's bin house looks nice, but it's a hygiene nightmare in August. We must avoid that.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Guys, the costs are scary! A new shelter is way too expensive, even with the subsidy. We're talking tens of thousands of yen per house.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried. The records show that even with a structure, people still fight over the smallest things, like who cleans the floor. We need a gentle approach.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,I have found that the paperwork is a heavy chain. A permanent structure requires months of waiting and constant signatures. It is a burden on the spirit.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Kenji, I don't care about the cost if it means we stop exploiting one neighbor's frontage. We can't just keep it where it is.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, but if we build a shelter that traps smells, we're just swapping a visual eyesore for a scent that makes the corner unbearable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"But we're already spending thirty-four thousand yen a year on ""band-aid"" fixes! We're losing money every year by not having a proper system.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Midori,,"If we choose a system that requires one person to ""supervise"" or ""manage,"" I fear it will only create more resentment between us.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Midori is correct. My research shows that ""supervision"" takes nearly an hour per session. Over a year, that is a theft of time we cannot recover.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"Then we rotate! If the space is the issue, we rotate the location. But wait, some frontages are too narrow. We need a plan that accounts for that.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"Rotation sounds fair on paper, but imagine the chaos of moving the point every month. It's the daily consistency that prevents friction.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"If we can't afford a big shelter, maybe we can find a cheaper way to organize it that still stops the waste of money on nets and deodorants.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I just want us to be able to talk to each other again. If we pick a ""fair"" option that is too strict, we'll just find new things to fight about.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"Let us remember that the simplest path is often the most sustainable. If the administration is too complex, the system will collapse under its own weight.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
