60,3,1,talk,May,,Option A is the only one that addresses the unfairness of the current location. I won't vote for anything that leaves it at one person's gate.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,I strongly oppose Option C. I've seen the bin house at the station block; it's a breeding ground for smells in the summer. It's a mistake.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Option C is way too expensive! Even with the subsidy, it's a huge hit to our budgets. I can't support a plan that costs us that much.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Option B sounds like it would create a ""police"" atmosphere. I don't want us monitoring each other's timing; it will only lead to more arguments.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,Option B is a trap of time. Spending an hour every few weeks to watch a bin is a waste of a human life. We must avoid it.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Mizuki, @Kenji, you both hate Option C, and @Midori and @Servas hate Option B. It seems we are all leaning toward Option A.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Kenji"",""Midori"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"Option A is not perfect, but it's the most logical. It avoids the hygiene trap of a shelter and the social tension of ""supervision.""","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I'm okay with Option A. It doesn't cost us a huge amount of money upfront, and it's fair because everyone shares the burden of the space.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Midori,,"I worry that moving the bins might cause new disputes, but it's better than the tension of a ""manager"" or the cost of a shelter.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,Rotation is a natural cycle. It teaches us to walk in each other's shoes—literally. It is the most philosophical and fair approach.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,I'm glad we agree. Let's just make sure the rotation accounts for the narrow frontages so we don't block the whole sidewalk.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"As long as we keep the area clean and don't build something that traps odors, I can live with the rotation. It's the most hygienic choice.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Kenji,,And it saves us from a massive bill! We can use a tiny bit of our budget for better signage so the truck driver doesn't get confused.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Midori,,I feel much better knowing we've reached a consensus. I think this will help us start talking to each other as neighbors again.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"When we share the burden, the burden becomes light. This is the path to a peaceful neighborhood. I am satisfied with this choice.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
